$ python3 scripts/android_wifi_preflight.py --help
usage: android_wifi_preflight.py [-h] [--adb ADB] [--ssid SSID]
                                 [--security {open,owe,wpa2,wpa3}]
                                 [--expected-subnet EXPECTED_SUBNET]
                                 [--expected-host EXPECTED_HOST]
                                 [--device DEVICE] [--check-only]
                                 [--wait-seconds WAIT_SECONDS]
                                 [--timeout TIMEOUT]

Verify and optionally provision Android Wi-Fi for HydraCam.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --adb ADB             Path to adb. Defaults to Android SDK platform-tools.
  --ssid SSID           Target SSID. May also be set with HYDRACAM_WIFI_SSID.
  --security {open,owe,wpa2,wpa3}
                        Target network security type for Android cmd wifi.
  --expected-subnet EXPECTED_SUBNET
                        Expected HydraCam LAN subnet, for example
                        192.168.178.0/24. Use auto to infer it from the Mac
                        route to --expected-host.
  --expected-host EXPECTED_HOST
                        Host used when --expected-subnet=auto. Use a known
                        device bridge IP, such as a reachable iPhone
                        automation host, when available.
  --device DEVICE       ADB serial to include. Repeat to select multiple
                        devices.
  --check-only          Inspect devices without attempting to connect or
                        opening settings.
  --wait-seconds WAIT_SECONDS
                        Seconds to wait for a provisioned device to receive a
                        wlan0 route.
  --timeout TIMEOUT     Per-adb-command timeout in seconds.
[exit-code] 0

